# code.gs contracts

Match the existing `var` / `function` style. Sheet names are exact: `scheme_codes`, `nav_data`, and `fund_selection` when that sheet is present.

## Entry points — do not rename
`onOpen` menu **Mutual Fund Matrix**; `showDialog` (1250×820); `doGet` (viewport meta, not embeddable); `getFundMatrixData(params)`; `getFundPublishedProfile`; `getFundOverlap`; `getSipTransactions`. There is no sidebar. `getSipTransactions` runs only when a Transactions link is opened.

Every other function name ends with `_`. Apps Script lets the browser call any function that does not end with `_`, running as the spreadsheet owner. Do not add a public function, and do not remove the trailing `_`.

## Sheet access
`appsscript.json` grants `spreadsheets.currentonly`, the container UI, and external fetch. `getActiveSpreadsheet` rejects `spreadsheets.readonly`. `currentonly` is limited to this bound spreadsheet. Do not add the full `spreadsheets` scope or any `setValue`, `appendRow`, `clear`, or `protect` call. The web app runs as the owner and is limited to that owner. A new deployment is required after this manifest changes.

## NAV
`loadNavIndex_` reads `nav_data` once per call and keeps only scheme codes listed on `scheme_codes`. Match by `scheme_code`, not by fund name. `lookupNav_` is the last NAV on or before the day, using the spreadsheet timezone so the calendar date matches the cell. Do not round that NAV. `units × NAV`, invested, corpus, profit, and lot gains stay exact. Whole-rupee rounding happens when a total is shown. Do not synthesize NAV. Do not cache the sheet in `CacheService`.

## Fund lists
`fund_selection` columns are `list_name`, `scheme_code`, `scheme_name`. When the sheet has rows, those lists replace the built-in Ran, Man, Sai, Best of One Per Category, Best of Two Per Category, Best of Mid & Small, and Only of International Category sets. A partial `scheme_name` matches one `scheme_codes` row. The screen uses that scheme’s real name. A name that matches nothing is reported and left out. Sai stays an empty list until rows are added.

## Params
`sipAmount` (1000), `sipDay` (1–31, default 5), `fromDate` (today minus 1 year), `toDate` (today), `saleDate` (today). Dates are `yyyy-MM-dd`. If `sipDay` is missing in a month, that installment is the 1st of the next month. Units are bought at the first published NAV on or after that day.

Custom range: one SIP on `sipDay` each month from From through To, redeemed at the To Date NAV. Fields: `customRangeXirr`, `sipCorpus`, `netProfit`, `absoluteReturn`, `navStart`, `navEnd`, `units`, `investedAmount`. `redeem` splits that SIP into lots held 12 months or more (`ltcgGain`) and younger lots (`stcgGain`, plus `exitLoad` at 1% of those lots' value). `switchPath` is 36 month-end 3-year CAGRs ending on Sale Date, aligned with `pathMonths`. `saleNav` is the Sale Date NAV and is not an input to the custom range.

## Tenures (`TENURE_CONFIG`)
Calendar lookbacks from Sale Date, not fixed day counts. Short: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y`. Long: `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y` `15Y`. `7Y` is intentional.
`tenureXirr` is an annualized Newton XIRR on a 365.25-day year, including 1M–9M. That is why those cells read higher than the period's price change. It is `null` when the fund has no NAV on or before the window start, or when the window has no SIP date. `5D` and `15D` are always null for XIRR. Do not relabel a shorter history as a full tenure.
`tenureCagr` is the point-to-point NAV change. Under 1Y it is absolute. From 1Y it is annualized with 365.25. It can be present when XIRR is null.
`tenureAbsolute` is that same point-to-point change with no annualizing, on every tenure including 1Y and longer. 5D and 15D are filled. A missing start NAV leaves the cell null.
Keep this order identical to the client `TENURES` array.

## Risk (`fund.risk`)
Three years of daily NAV ending on Sale Date. Cash rate `0.065`. `volatility` is annualized standard deviation. Also `downsideDeviation`, `sharpe`, `sortino`, `treynor`, `maxDrawdown`, `maxDrawup`, `bestMonth`, `worstMonth`, `var95` (5th percentile of daily returns), `rollingReturn`, and `rollingHit` (share of monthly 1-year windows that were positive, over about four years). `upsideCapture`, `downsideCapture`, `beta`, `alpha`, `informationRatio`, `rSquared`, `correlation`, `trackingError`, and `trackingDifference` use the other tracked funds in the same category, not an index. Expense ratio stays on `getFundPublishedProfile` and is null when that call fails. Do not invent published fields.

## Overlap (`getFundOverlap`)
At most 20 `{ code, name }` rows. Fetches the latest published equity book and returns pairwise overlap as a fraction of the portfolio: sum of the smaller weight of each shared stock, divided by 100. Match the published scheme code before using holdings. Cash and debt are excluded. A missing portfolio is an error on that fund, not a zero book.
